${"##"} Terms

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `n` | MIO peripheral input, from 0 to `NMioPeriphIn` - 1 |
| `k` | MIO peripheral output, from 0 to `NMioPeriphOut` - 1 |
| `p` | MIO pad, from 0 to `NMioPads` - 1 |
| `d` | DIO pad, from 0 to `NDioPads` - 1 |
| Watched signal | The pad input that `MIODIO` and `PADSEL` pick |
| Forwarded value | The watched signal sampled each `clk_aon_i` cycle, through the filter when `FILTER` is 1 |
| Asleep, awake | A pad is asleep while its sleep status bit is 1, awake while it is 0 |
| AON | The always-on domain: the logic on `clk_aon_i` and `rst_aon_ni` |
| Lands | A written or sampled value lands in the cycle the register or flop it is meant for takes it |
| Hardware write | A write to a register field made by the pinmux logic, not by software over the bus |
% if strap:
| Full reset | A reset that asserts `rst_sys_ni`, which the top connects to the system reset tree ([top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson)) |
% endif
% if strap:
| NDM reset | A reset that asserts `rst_ni` and `rst_aon_ni`, and not `rst_sys_ni`. ${'The top connects `rst_ni` and `rst_aon_ni` to the life cycle reset tree' if not aon_on_sys else 'This top connects `rst_ni` to the life cycle reset tree and `rst_aon_ni` to the system reset tree'} ([top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson)). ${'A non-debug module reset request asserts that tree outside PROD and PROD_END' if dm_top else 'This top has no debug module, so no non-debug module reset request occurs on it. On a top with one, the request asserts the life cycle reset tree outside PROD and PROD_END'} ([Summary](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#summary)). A flop on `rst_sys_ni` keeps its value through this reset (${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset)) |
% endif
% if strap:
| Steadily On | An input is steadily On in a cycle when the input was On, and the design was out of full reset, in each of the two cycles before that cycle |
% endif
% if strap:
| On, Off | On is 4'b0101 and Off 4'b1010, the life cycle controller's values ([Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation)) |
% endif
% if strap:
| The latch | The latched debug enable, seen on `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` and through the RISC-V TAP |
% endif
% if strap:
| A clear | `lc_hw_debug_clr_i`, `lc_check_byp_en_i` or `lc_escalate_en_i` at any value other than Off (${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation) for the debug clear and the escalation input); it turns the latch Off |
% endif
% if strap:
| Connected | A TAP is connected while the TAP straps name it and its gate is open: the life cycle TAP at straps 01; the RISC-V TAP at straps 10 while the latch is On; the DFT TAP at straps 11 while `lc_dft_en_i` is On; on a top with the RRAM TAP (`enable_rram_tap`), the RRAM TAP at straps 00 while `RRAM_JTAG_SEL` is `kMultiBitBool4True` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` is On; at straps 00, no TAP otherwise ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation), ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset)) |
% endif
% if strap:
| Owns | A TAP owns the JTAG pads while it is connected: the pads then carry the TAP's signals, not what the pad muxes select |
% endif
% if strap:
| Cut | A TAP is cut while its gate is shut, or while the TAP straps name another TAP or none |
% endif
| Allowed pad | A pad is allowed for a signal when the signal's pad list names the pad, or when the list is empty. The pad list is the signal's `pads` entry in the top's configuration ([top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) `mio_periph_ins`; [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) `mio_periph_outs`). |

