${"##"} Input selection

Conditions:

* ${'Every row holds in every cycle, except for a JTAG pad while a TAP owns it.' if strap else 'Every row holds in every cycle.'}
* An input's pad list limits only the select values that name a pad.
* The constant selects 0 and 1 act the same on every input, with or without a pad list.

Testpoints: [`pad_listen`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#pad_listen) (V1, priority 1), [`reset_state`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#reset_state) (V2, priority 2), [`sparse_insel`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#sparse_insel) (V2, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_in_01"></a>REQ_IN_01 | <br>MIO peripheral input `n` shall read 0 while `MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_n` is 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_listen`: *reads tie 0*. In every cycle the check compares each MIO peripheral input whose select is 0 with 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_02"></a>REQ_IN_02 | <br>MIO peripheral input `n` shall read 1 while `MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_n` is 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_listen`: *reads tie 1*. In every cycle the check compares each MIO peripheral input whose select is 1 with 1.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_03"></a>REQ_IN_03 | <br>MIO peripheral input `n` shall read the input of MIO pad `p`, in the same cycle, while `MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_n` is 2 + `p` and pad `p` is allowed for input `n`. Here `p` runs from 0 to `NMioPads` - 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel); [Muxing Matrix](../theory_of_operation.md#muxing-matrix); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_pads`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `mio_periph_ins`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_listen`: *reads selected pad*. The check compares each MIO peripheral input with `mio_in_i[p]` in the same cycle while its select is 2 + `p`, for every `p` from 0 to `NMioPads` - 1. For an input with a pad list, the check runs only over the pads that the list allows.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_04"></a>REQ_IN_04 | <br>MIO peripheral input `n` shall read 0 while `MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_n` is greater than `NMioPads` + 1. These select values name no pad. (*RTL*) <br><br>*Sources:* No specification states this rule. Nearest text: [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_pads`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_listen`: *select without a pad reads 0*. While the select of a MIO peripheral input is greater than `NMioPads` + 1, the check compares the input with 0. These select values name no pad.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_05"></a>REQ_IN_05 | <br>DIO peripheral input `d` shall read the input of DIO pad `d`, in the same cycle, at every value of the pinmux registers. <br><br>*Sources:* [MIO and DIO Signal Categories](../theory_of_operation.md#mio-and-dio-signal-categories)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_listen`: *DIO reads its pad*. The check compares each DIO peripheral input with its own pad's bit of `dio_in_i` in the same cycle, at every value of the registers.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_06"></a>REQ_IN_06 | <br>After reset and until software writes its select, MIO peripheral input `n` shall read the pad input or the constant 0 or 1 that the top defines as its reset selection. An input with no reset selection defined shall read 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [Pinmux Configuration](../programmers_guide.md#pinmux-configuration); [MIO and DIO Signal Categories](../theory_of_operation.md#mio-and-dio-signal-categories); [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `mio_periph_ins`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `reset_state`: *input starts at default*. From reset until the input's select is written, the check compares the input with the input's default value in every cycle. For an input with no default, the check compares the input with 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_in_07"></a>REQ_IN_07 | <br>MIO peripheral input `n` shall read 0 while `MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_n` is 2 + `p` and pad `p` is not allowed for input `n`. <br><br>*Sources:* [Muxing Matrix](../theory_of_operation.md#muxing-matrix); [Pinmux Configuration](../programmers_guide.md#pinmux-configuration); [`MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN`](../registers.md#mio_periph_insel); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `mio_periph_ins`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `sparse_insel`: *unlisted pad reads zero*. While the input select names a pad that the input's pad list does not allow, the check compares the input with 0 in the same cycle.<br><br> |

${"##"} Output selection

Conditions:

* ${'Every row holds while the pad is awake and no TAP owns the pad.' if strap else 'Every row holds while the pad is awake.'}
* A pad list limits only the select values that name a peripheral output, so the constant select values 0, 1 and 2 behave the same on every pad.

Testpoints: [`pad_output`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#pad_output) (V1, priority 1), [`reset_state`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#reset_state) (V2, priority 2), [`sparse_outsel`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#sparse_outsel) (V2, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_out_01a"></a>REQ_OUT_01a | <br>The output of MIO pad `p` shall be 0 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *tie 0 drives 0*. While an awake pad's select is 0, the check compares the pad's output with 0 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_01b"></a>REQ_OUT_01b | <br>The output enable of MIO pad `p` shall be 1 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 0, so the pad drives 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *tie 0 drives 0*. While an awake pad's select is 0, the check compares the pad's output enable with 1 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_02a"></a>REQ_OUT_02a | <br>The output of MIO pad `p` shall be 1 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *tie 1 drives 1*. While an awake pad's select is 1, the check compares the pad's output with 1 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_02b"></a>REQ_OUT_02b | <br>The output enable of MIO pad `p` shall be 1 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 1, so the pad drives 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *tie 1 drives 1*. While an awake pad's select is 1, the check compares the pad's output enable with 1 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_03a"></a>REQ_OUT_03a | <br>The output enable of MIO pad `p` shall be 0 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 2, so the pad is high-Z. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *select 2 is high-Z*. While an awake pad's select is 2, the check compares the pad's output enable with 0 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_03b"></a>REQ_OUT_03b | <br>The output of MIO pad `p` shall be 0 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 2. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *select 2 is high-Z*. While an awake pad's select is 2, the check compares the pad's output with 0 in every cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_04a"></a>REQ_OUT_04a | <br>MIO pad `p` shall carry peripheral output `k`, in the same cycle, while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 3 + `k` and pad `p` is allowed for output `k`. Here `k` runs from 0 to `NMioPeriphOut` - 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel); [Muxing Matrix](../theory_of_operation.md#muxing-matrix); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_periph_out`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `mio_periph_outs`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *drives selected output*. While an awake pad's select is 3 + `k`, the check compares its output with `periph_to_mio_i[k]` in the same cycle, for `k` from 0 to `NMioPeriphOut` - 1. On a top with pad lists, the check skips outputs not allowed for the pad.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_04b"></a>REQ_OUT_04b | <br>MIO pad `p` shall carry output enable `k`, in the same cycle, while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is 3 + `k` and pad `p` is allowed for output `k`. Here `k` runs from 0 to `NMioPeriphOut` - 1. <br><br>*Sources:* [`MIO_OUTSEL.OUT`](../registers.md#mio_outsel); [Muxing Matrix](../theory_of_operation.md#muxing-matrix); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_periph_out`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `mio_periph_outs`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *drives selected output*. While an awake pad's select is 3 + `k`, the check compares its output enable with `periph_to_mio_oe_i[k]` in the same cycle, for `k` from 0 to `NMioPeriphOut` - 1. On a top with pad lists, the check skips outputs not allowed for the pad.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_out_05a"></a>REQ_OUT_05a | <br>The output enable of MIO pad `p` shall be 0 while `MIO_OUTSEL_p` is greater than `NMioPeriphOut` + 2, so the pad is high-Z. These select values name no peripheral output.${'' if outsel_spare else ' On this top, `MIO_OUTSEL_p` has no value greater than `NMioPeriphOut` + 2, so this row does not apply.'} (*RTL*) <br><br>*Sources:* No specification states this rule. Nearest text: [`MIO_OUTSEL`](../registers.md#mio_outsel); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_periph_out`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `pad_output`: *select without an output is high-Z*. While an awake pad's select is greater than `NMioPeriphOut` + 2, the check compares the pad's output enable with 0. These select values name no peripheral output.<br><br> |
