| <a id="req_usb_04a"></a>REQ_USB_04a | <br>The module shall run on `clk_aon_i`. <br><br>*Sources:* [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[USB Wakeup Detection Module](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#usb-wakeup-detection-module); [AON/Wake Clocking](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-clocking); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_conn`: *module on AON clock*. The check compares the module's clock with `clk_aon_i` in every cycle. The proofs clock `clk_aon_i` slower than `clk_i`, so a module on `clk_i` fails the check.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_04b"></a>REQ_USB_04b | <br>The module shall be reset by `rst_aon_ni`. <br><br>*Sources:* [pinmux.hjson `clocking`](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [AON/Wake Clocking](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-clocking)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_conn`: *module on AON reset*. The check requires `rst_aon_ni` to drive the reset pin of every flop of the module.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_05a"></a>REQ_USB_05a | <br>The module's D+ input shall be the signal that the pinmux delivers to usbdev as its D+ input. That signal is the input of the USB D+ pad, which is a DIO pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [AON/Wake Interface Pins](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-interface-pins); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinout.pads USB_P`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux.signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_conn`: *bus inputs*. The check compares the module's D+ input with the USB D+ pad in every cycle. An input taken from the USB D- pad, from another pad or through a flop fails the check.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_05b"></a>REQ_USB_05b | <br>The module's D- input shall be the signal that the pinmux delivers to usbdev as its D- input. That signal is the input of the USB D- pad, which is a DIO pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [AON/Wake Interface Pins](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-interface-pins); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinout.pads USB_N`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux.signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_conn`: *bus inputs*. The check compares the module's D- input with the USB D- pad in every cycle. An input taken from the USB D+ pad, from another pad or through a flop fails the check.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_05c"></a>REQ_USB_05c | <br>The module's VBUS input shall be the signal that the pinmux delivers to usbdev as its VBUS input. That signal is the muxed input `sense` after its input select. <br><br>*Sources:* [AON/Wake Interface Pins](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-interface-pins); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `pinmux.signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_conn`: *bus inputs*. The check compares the module's VBUS input with usbdev's sense input in every cycle. The check takes the sense input after its input select.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06a"></a>REQ_USB_06a | <br>While the module is inactive, a suspend request shall make it active within a bounded time. (*RTL*: the length of the bound) <br><br>*Sources:* [Suspending](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#suspending); [usbdev.hjson `wake_control.suspend_req`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the length of the bound.<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *request activates*. The check requires `usbdev_wake_detect_active` to be 1 within 2 AON clock cycles of each suspend request that comes while the module is inactive.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06b"></a>REQ_USB_06b | <br>While the module is active, a wake acknowledge shall make it inactive within a bounded time. (*RTL*: the length of the bound) <br><br>*Sources:* [Resuming](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#resuming); [usbdev.hjson `wake_control.wake_ack`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the length of the bound.<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *acknowledge releases*. The check requires `usbdev_wake_detect_active` to be 0 within 2 AON clock cycles of each wake acknowledge that comes while the module is active.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06c"></a>REQ_USB_06c | <br>Only a suspend request made while the module is inactive shall make the module active. Only a wake acknowledge made while the module is active shall make the module inactive. <br><br>*Sources:* [Suspending](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#suspending); [Resuming](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#resuming); [usbdev.hjson `wake_control.suspend_req`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [usbdev.hjson `wake_control.wake_ack`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *no other state change*. The check allows `usbdev_wake_detect_active` to rise only after a suspend request, and to fall only after a wake acknowledge.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06d"></a>REQ_USB_06d | <br>While the module is inactive, each pad pull-up enable (`usb_dppullup_en` and `usb_dnpullup_en`) shall equal usbdev's pull-up enable for the same line, in the same cycle. <br><br>*Sources:* [AON/Wake Interface Pins](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-interface-pins); [Resuming](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#resuming); [usbdev.hjson `wake_control.wake_ack`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *inactive passes pull-ups*. In every cycle that the module is inactive, the check compares each pull-up enable to the pads with usbdev's enable of the same line.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06e"></a>REQ_USB_06e | <br>While the module is active and `usbdev_sense_lost` is 0, each pad pull-up enable shall keep the value that usbdev's pull-up enable for the same line had at the suspend request that made the module active. <br><br>*Sources:* [Overview](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#overview); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[chip_usbdev_testplan.hjson `chip_sw_usbdev_aon_pullup`](../../../../../top_earlgrey/data/ip/chip_usbdev_testplan.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *active holds pull-ups*, *pull-ups after VBUS loss* (waits on a specification question). In every cycle that the module is active and `usbdev_sense_lost` is 0, the check requires each pull-up enable to the pads to equal usbdev's enable of its line at the suspend request. No specification says what the pull-ups do after VBUS is lost.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06f"></a>REQ_USB_06f | <br>While the module is active, each of three conditions that is held on the USB lines shall set its event within a bounded time. The three conditions are bus not idle, bus reset (D+ and D- both low) and sense lost (VBUS low). (*RTL*: the length of the bound, and the idle state of the lines while no pull-up enable is 1 or both are 1) <br><br>*Sources:* [Optional external AON/Wake functionality](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#optional-external-aonwake-functionality); [AON/Wake Clocking](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-clocking); [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.disconnected`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.bus_reset`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.bus_not_idle`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_resume`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_reset`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_disconnect`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the length of the bound, and the idle state of the lines while no pull-up enable is 1 or both are 1.<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *held condition sets event*. The check requires each event to be 1 once its condition has been on the USB lines in one cycle and in each of the 8 cycles after it.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06g"></a>REQ_USB_06g | <br>The module shall set an event only after the event's own condition has been on the USB lines, with the module active, for at least the shortest time that the module must report. <br><br>*Sources:* [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.disconnected`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.bus_reset`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [usbdev.hjson `wake_events.bus_not_idle`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [AON/Wake Clocking](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/theory_of_operation.md#aonwake-clocking); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *event only after its condition*, *short condition sets no event* (waits on a specification question). The check allows an event to rise only on its own condition. The condition must be seen while the module is active, and the module must stay active from then until the rise. No specification gives the shortest time that a condition must last.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06h"></a>REQ_USB_06h | <br>An event, once set, shall stay set for as long as the module stays active. <br><br>*Sources:* [Resuming](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#resuming); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *event holds while active*. The check requires an event that is 1 to stay 1 in the next cycle while the module stays active. The check applies at every value of the USB lines.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06i"></a>REQ_USB_06i | <br>A wake acknowledge made while the module is active shall clear each of the three events within a bounded time. (*RTL*: the length of the bound) <br><br>*Sources:* [Resuming](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#resuming); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the length of the bound.<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *acknowledge clears events*. After each wake acknowledge that comes while the module is active, the check requires each of the three events to be 0 in one of the next 4 AON clock cycles.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_usb_06j"></a>REQ_USB_06j | <br>The module's wake request shall be 1 while at least one of its three events is set, and 0 while none of them is set. (*RTL*: the delay from the events to the request) <br><br>*Sources:* [Overview](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/wake_resume.md#overview); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_resume`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_reset`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [usbdev_testplan.hjson `aon_wake_disconnect`](../../../../../ip/usbdev/data/usbdev_testplan.hjson); [Inter-Module Signals](../../../../../ip/usbdev/doc/interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [Wakeup Recording](../../../pwrmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-recording); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_usb_wakeup`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the delay from the events to the request.<br><br>*Checked by:* `usb_module`: *wake request follows events*. The check compares `usb_wkup_req` with the three events in every cycle. The check requires `usb_wkup_req` to be 1 when at least one event is 1, and 0 when none is.<br><br> |
% endif
