${"##"} Strap sampling

Security-relevant ([Groups](#groups)).

Conditions:

* The TAP straps are seen through the TAP that is connected ([TAP selection and the JTAG pads](#tap-selection-and-the-jtag-pads)).
* Full reset and NDM reset are defined in the [Terms](#terms).
* The life cycle conditions follow the table of life cycle states ([Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)), after the delay of the input synchronizers.
* The top description assigns the TAP strap 0 pad and the TAP strap 1 pad, which the table [Pads by role](#pads-by-role) lists.

Testpoints: [`strap`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#strap) (V2S, priority 1).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_strap_01"></a>REQ_STRAP_01 | <br>At each `strap_en_i` pulse, TAP strap 0 shall take the value of the TAP strap 0 pad, if `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0. This holds in every life cycle state. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap0`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *pulse samples the straps*. The check compares strap 0 after a strap pulse with the TAP strap 0 pad. The check accepts the value of the pad in the pulse cycle or in the cycle after it.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_02a"></a>REQ_STRAP_02a | <br>At a `strap_en_i` pulse, TAP strap 1 shall take the value of the TAP strap 1 pad, if `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0 and `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is On. [`REQ_STRAP_03`](#req_strap_03) states the one exception. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap1`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *pulse samples the straps*. When `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is steadily On at a strap pulse, the check compares strap 1 after the pulse with the TAP strap 1 pad. The check accepts the value of the pad in the pulse cycle or in the cycle after it.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_02b"></a>REQ_STRAP_02b | <br>At each `strap_en_i` pulse, TAP strap 1 shall keep its value, if `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is not On. [`REQ_STRAP_03`](#req_strap_03) states the one exception. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tap1`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *pulse samples the straps*. When neither `lc_hw_debug_en_i` nor `lc_dft_en_i` was On before a strap pulse, the check requires strap 1 to be unchanged after the pulse.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_03"></a>REQ_STRAP_03 | <br>While `lc_dft_en_i` is On and `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0, each TAP strap shall take the value that its pad had in the cycle before. TAP strap 0 is sampled from the TAP strap 0 pad, and TAP strap 1 is sampled from the TAP strap 1 pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *straps follow the pads*. While `lc_dft_en_i` is steadily On, the check compares strap 0 with the value of the TAP strap 0 pad in the cycle before. The check compares strap 1 with the TAP strap 1 pad in the same way.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_04"></a>REQ_STRAP_04 | <br>While `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 1, the TAP straps shall keep their values. This holds at a `strap_en_i` pulse too. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *straps hold*. While `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 1, the check requires both straps to be unchanged in the next cycle. The check requires this at a strap pulse too, and while `lc_dft_en_i` is On.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_05"></a>REQ_STRAP_05 | <br>In a cycle without a `strap_en_i` pulse, the TAP straps shall keep their values. [`REQ_STRAP_03`](#req_strap_03) states the one exception, which applies while `lc_dft_en_i` is On and `dft_hold_tap_sel_i` is 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *straps hold*. The check applies in a cycle without a strap pulse when `lc_dft_en_i` was On in neither of the two cycles before. In such a cycle, the check requires both straps to be unchanged and allows the pads to take any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_06"></a>REQ_STRAP_06 | <br>A TAP strap that has not been sampled since the last full reset shall read 0. (*RTL*) <br><br>*Sources:* No specification states this rule. Nearest text: [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *unsampled strap reads 0*, *pulse samples the straps*, *straps hold*. The check _unsampled strap reads 0_ requires both straps to be 0 from a full reset until a sample. The other two checks require a strap 1 that was never sampled to stay at 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_07"></a>REQ_STRAP_07 | <br>An NDM reset shall leave both TAP straps unchanged. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Reset Request Handling](../../../pwrmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#reset-request-handling); [System Reset Tree](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#system-reset-tree); [Summary](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#summary); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *straps outside NDM reset*. The check fails when `rst_ni` or `rst_aon_ni` reaches the reset pin or the input cone of a flop that holds a sampled TAP strap. An NDM reset asserts these two resets.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_strap_08"></a>REQ_STRAP_08 | <br>While the parameter `SecVolatileRawUnlockEn` is 0, `strap_en_override_i` shall not change the straps. <br><br>*Sources:* [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `param_list` SecVolatileRawUnlockEn](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [Volatile `RAW` -> `TEST_UNLOCKED0` Transition](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/programmers_guide.md#volatile-raw---test_unlocked0-transition); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `strap`: *straps hold*. With `strap_en_override_i` free in every cycle, the check requires the straps to be unchanged in each cycle in which no sample is due.<br><br> |
% endif
% if strap:

${"##"} Latched debug enable

Security-relevant ([Groups](#groups)).

Conditions: The latch, On and Off are defined in the [Terms](#terms).

Testpoints: [`latch`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#latch) (V2S, priority 1).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_dbg_01a"></a>REQ_DBG_01a | <br>At each `strap_en_i` pulse, the latch shall take the value On if `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is On. [`REQ_DBG_09`](#req_dbg_09) states the one exception. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *pulse samples debug enable*. At a strap pulse with `lc_hw_debug_en_i` steadily On and the clear inputs at Off, the check compares `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` with On in the next cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_01b"></a>REQ_DBG_01b | <br>At each `strap_en_i` pulse, the latch shall take the value Off if `lc_hw_debug_en_i` is not On. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *pulse samples debug enable*, *On only at a pulse*. The check _pulse samples debug enable_ requires the latch to be Off after a strap pulse with the debug enable not On. The check _On only at a pulse_ allows a rise to On only at a strap pulse with the debug enable On.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_02"></a>REQ_DBG_02 | <br>The latch shall keep its value in each cycle with no `strap_en_i` pulse, no clear and no full reset. This holds through an NDM reset too. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [System Reset Tree](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#system-reset-tree); [Summary](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#summary); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *latch holds*, *latch outside NDM reset*. The check _latch holds_ requires the output to keep its value. The check _latch outside NDM reset_ fails when `rst_ni` or `rst_aon_ni`, which an NDM reset asserts, reaches the reset pin or input cone of a latch flop.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_03"></a>REQ_DBG_03 | <br>Any value other than Off on `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` shall turn the latch Off. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [lc_ctrl.hjson `inter_signal_list` lc_hw_debug_clr](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/data/lc_ctrl.hjson); [HW_DEBUG_CLR](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/theory_of_operation.md#hw_debug_clr); [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *clear turns Off*. The check requires the latch to be Off one cycle after `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` has held a value other than Off for two cycles. The value On counts as other than Off.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_04"></a>REQ_DBG_04 | <br>Any value other than Off on `lc_check_byp_en_i` shall turn the latch Off. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *clear turns Off*. The check requires the latch to be Off one cycle after `lc_check_byp_en_i` has held a value other than Off for two cycles. The value On counts as other than Off.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_05"></a>REQ_DBG_05 | <br>Any value other than Off on `lc_escalate_en_i` shall turn the latch Off. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *clear turns Off*. The check requires the latch to be Off one cycle after `lc_escalate_en_i` has held any of its 15 values other than Off for two cycles.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_06"></a>REQ_DBG_06 | <br>The value Off on `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` and on `lc_check_byp_en_i` shall not turn the latch Off. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *latch holds*, *pulse samples debug enable*. Both checks apply with `lc_hw_debug_clr_i` and `lc_check_byp_en_i` at Off. The checks require the output to hold outside a strap pulse (_latch holds_) and to be On after a sample of On (_pulse samples debug enable_).<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_07a"></a>REQ_DBG_07a | <br>`pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` shall be On while the latch is On. <br><br>*Sources:* [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` PINMUX_HW_DEBUG_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *output On or Off*, *pulse samples debug enable*, *latch holds*. The checks _pulse samples debug enable_ and _latch holds_ require the output to be On after a sample of On and while the latch holds On. The check _output On or Off_ rejects any value but On and Off.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_07b"></a>REQ_DBG_07b | <br>`pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` shall be Off while the latch is not On. <br><br>*Sources:* [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` PINMUX_HW_DEBUG_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *output On or Off*, *On only at a pulse*, *clear turns Off*. The check _output On or Off_ rejects any value but On and Off. The check _On only at a pulse_ rejects an On not taken at a strap pulse. The check _clear turns Off_ rejects any value but Off after a clear.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_08"></a>REQ_DBG_08 | <br>After a full reset, the latch shall be Off until the next `strap_en_i` pulse. <br><br>*Sources:* [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [lc_ctrl.hjson `inter_signal_list` lc_hw_debug_en](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/data/lc_ctrl.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *Off from full reset*, *On only at a pulse*. The check _Off from full reset_ requires the latch to be Off in full reset. The check _On only at a pulse_ rejects any rise to On before a strap pulse at which the debug enable is On.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dbg_09"></a>REQ_DBG_09 | <br>A clear in the same cycle as a `strap_en_i` pulse shall leave the latch Off. <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `latch`: *clear turns Off*. The check applies to a strap pulse when a clear input held a value other than Off in both of the two cycles before the pulse. The check then requires the latch to be Off in the next cycle, even with `lc_hw_debug_en_i` On.<br><br> |
