${"##"} TAP selection and the JTAG pads

Security-relevant ([Groups](#groups)).

Conditions:

* The JTAG pads are the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad, the TRST_N pad and the TDO pad, which the top description assigns ([top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson)) and the table [Pads by role](#pads-by-role) lists.
* The rows hold once the TAP straps and the life cycle inputs have kept their values for the delay of the input synchronizers.
* The rows do not hold for TRST_N while scan mode is on.
* Two documents disagree on the attributes of a JTAG pad that a TAP owns.
* The theory of operation says "all-zero" ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation)), and the assertion `MioJtagAttrO_A` of the existing testplan keeps the Schmitt trigger on.
* [REQ_TAP_08](#req_tap_08) follows the theory of operation.

Testpoints: [`jtag`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#jtag) (V2S, priority 1), [`jtag_pad`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#jtag_pad) (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_tap_01a"></a>REQ_TAP_01a | <br>While the TAP straps are 01, the TCK of `lc_jtag_o` shall carry the input of the TCK pad, in every life cycle state. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.lc_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. The check compares the `tck` field of `lc_jtag_o` with the TCK pad in the same cycle. The check does this in every life cycle state and in scan mode.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_01b"></a>REQ_TAP_01b | <br>While the TAP straps are 01, the TMS of `lc_jtag_o` shall carry the input of the TMS pad, in every life cycle state. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.lc_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. The check compares the `tms` field of `lc_jtag_o` with the TMS pad in the same cycle. The check does this in every life cycle state and in scan mode.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_01c"></a>REQ_TAP_01c | <br>While the TAP straps are 01, the TDI of `lc_jtag_o` shall carry the input of the TDI pad, in every life cycle state. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.lc_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. The check compares the `tdi` field of `lc_jtag_o` with the TDI pad in the same cycle. The check does this in every life cycle state and in scan mode.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_01d"></a>REQ_TAP_01d | <br>While the TAP straps are 01, the TRST_N of `lc_jtag_o` shall carry the input of the TRST_N pad, in every life cycle state. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.lc_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. Outside scan mode, the check compares the `trst_n` field of `lc_jtag_o` with the TRST_N pad in the same cycle. In scan mode, no specification names the reset that `trst_n` follows.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_02a"></a>REQ_TAP_02a | <br>While the TAP straps are 10 and the latch is On, `rv_jtag_o` shall carry the inputs of the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rv_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. With TAP straps 10 and `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` On, the check compares `rv_jtag_o` with the JTAG pads in the same cycle. The check compares the `trst_n` field only outside scan mode.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_02b"></a>REQ_TAP_02b | <br>While the TAP straps are 10 and the latch is Off, `rv_jtag_o` shall not carry the inputs of the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rv_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *cut TAP gets zero*. With TAP straps 10 and `pinmux_hw_debug_en_o` Off, the check requires all four fields of `rv_jtag_o` to be 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_03a"></a>REQ_TAP_03a | <br>While the TAP straps are 11 and `lc_dft_en_i` is On, `dft_jtag_o` shall carry the inputs of the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` TAP.MUX.LC_GATED](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.top`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*. With TAP straps 11 and `lc_dft_en_i` steadily On, the check compares `dft_jtag_o` with the JTAG pads in the same cycle. The check compares the `trst_n` field only outside scan mode.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_03b"></a>REQ_TAP_03b | <br>While the TAP straps are 11 and `lc_dft_en_i` is Off, `dft_jtag_o` shall not carry the inputs of the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` TAP.MUX.LC_GATED](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.top`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *cut TAP gets zero*. With TAP straps 11 and `lc_dft_en_i` On in neither of the two cycles before, the check requires `dft_jtag_o` to be all 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_04"></a>REQ_TAP_04 | <br>The life cycle TAP, the RISC-V TAP and the DFT TAP shall each receive an all-zero request while that TAP is not connected. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.top`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *cut TAP gets zero*. The check applies to the life cycle, RISC-V and DFT TAPs in every cycle and at every scan mode value. In a cycle in which one of these TAPs is cut, the check requires all four fields of its request to be 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_05"></a>REQ_TAP_05 | <br>In strap sampling, in the latch and in TAP selection, `lc_dft_en_i` and `lc_hw_debug_en_i` shall count as On only at the value 4'b0101. <br><br>*Sources:* [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` LC_DFT_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *only On opens*, *cut TAP gets zero*; `strap`: *pulse samples the straps*, *straps hold*; `latch`: *pulse samples debug enable*. Each of these checks counts an enable as On only at the value 4'b0101.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_06a"></a>REQ_TAP_06a | <br>While a TAP is connected, the TDO pad shall drive the TDO of that TAP. <br><br>*Sources:* [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tdo`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [JTAG](../../../../../ip/rv_dm/doc/interfaces.md#jtag); [Security Countermeasures](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#security-countermeasures); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag_pad`: *TDO pad drives the TAP*. While the TDO pad is awake, the check compares ${"the pad's bit of `mio_out_o` with the `tdo`" if not jtag_dio else "the pad's bit of `mio_out_o` (`dio_out_o` for a DIO pad) with the `tdo`"} of the connected TAP in the same cycle.${' The RRAM TAP is included.' if rram else ''}<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_06b"></a>REQ_TAP_06b | <br>While a TAP is connected, the TDO pad shall take its output enable from that TAP. <br><br>*Sources:* [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals tdo`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [JTAG](../../../../../ip/rv_dm/doc/interfaces.md#jtag); [Security Countermeasures](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#security-countermeasures); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag_pad`: *TDO pad drives the TAP*. While the TDO pad is awake, the check compares ${"the pad's bit of `mio_oe_o` with the `tdo_oe`" if not jtag_dio else "the pad's bit of `mio_oe_o` (`dio_oe_o` for a DIO pad) with the `tdo_oe`"} of the connected TAP in the same cycle.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_07"></a>REQ_TAP_07 | <br>While a TAP is connected, the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad shall have output enable 0. <br><br>*Sources:* The TAPs' standard JTAG port takes TCK, TMS, TRST_N and TDI as pad inputs and drives only TDO and its enable ([JTAG](../../../../../ip/rv_dm/doc/interfaces.md#jtag); [Security Countermeasures](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#security-countermeasures))${on(rram, "; the RRAM TAP's port has the same JTAG type ([Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals)) and takes the JTAG IOs ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation))")}; [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag_pad`: *input pads not driven*. While a TAP is connected and the pads are awake, the check ${'requires `mio_oe_o` to be 0 for the TMS, TDI, TCK and TRST_N pads' if not jtag_dio else "requires the pad's bit of `mio_oe_o` (`dio_oe_o` for a DIO pad) to be 0 for the TMS, TDI, TCK and TRST_N pads"}. The check allows the output selects of these pads to hold any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_08"></a>REQ_TAP_08 | <br>While a TAP is connected, every attribute of the five JTAG pads shall be 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag_pad`: *JTAG attributes zero*. While a TAP is connected and the pads are awake, the check ${'requires every field of `mio_attr_o` to be 0 on the five JTAG pads' if not jtag_dio else "requires every field of the pad's entry of `mio_attr_o` (`dio_attr_o` for a DIO pad) to be 0 on the five JTAG pads"}. The check allows the attribute registers of these pads to hold any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_09"></a>REQ_TAP_09 | <br>Connecting a TAP shall not change the JTAG pads' attribute registers. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag_pad`: *attribute registers untouched*. In every cycle, the check allows the attribute read-back of each JTAG pad to change only by a software write.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_tap_12"></a>REQ_TAP_12 | <br>An NDM reset with no clear shall leave a connected RISC-V TAP connected. <br><br>*Sources:* [Life Cycle Control](../../../../../ip/rv_dm/doc/interfaces.md#life-cycle-control); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [lc_ctrl.hjson `inter_signal_list` lc_hw_debug_en](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/data/lc_ctrl.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rv_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [System Reset Tree](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#system-reset-tree); [Summary](../../../rstmgr/doc/theory_of_operation.md#summary)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *TAP selection outside NDM reset*, *connected TAP gets the pads*, *cut TAP gets zero*. The structure check requires that an NDM reset reaches no flop of the TAP selection. The `jtag` checks require that the state of these flops alone picks the connected TAP.<br><br> |
% endif
