${"##"} RRAM TAP

Security-relevant ([Groups](#groups)).

Conditions:

* These rows apply to a top that has the RRAM TAP ([top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson) `enable_rram_tap`).
* On a top without the RRAM TAP, TAP straps at 00 select no TAP ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation)).
* The JTAG pad rows of [TAP selection and the JTAG pads](#tap-selection-and-the-jtag-pads) also hold for the RRAM TAP while it is connected.
* No row covers the TRST_N of the RRAM TAP while scan mode is on ([Out of scope](README.md#out-of-scope)).
* The rows hold once the TAP straps and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` have kept their values for the delay of the input synchronizers.
* In [`REQ_RRAM_01`](#req_rram_01), TCK and TRST_N follow the TCK pad and the TRST_N pad from the second `clk_i` cycle in which the RRAM TAP is connected.

Testpoints: [`rram_tap`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#rram_tap) (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_rram_01"></a>REQ_RRAM_01 | <br>While the TAP straps are 00, `rram_jtag_o` shall carry the inputs of the TCK pad, the TMS pad, the TDI pad and the TRST_N pad, if `RRAM_JTAG_SEL` is `kMultiBitBool4True` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` is On. (*RTL*: the values of TCK and TRST_N in the first `clk_i` cycle of a connection) <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` TAP.MUX.LC_GATED](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `inter_module.connect pinmux.rram_jtag`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the values of TCK and TRST_N in the first `clk_i` cycle of a connection.<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *connected RRAM TAP gets the pads*. While the RRAM TAP is connected, the check compares `rram_jtag_o` with the TCK, TMS, TDI and TRST_N pads in the same cycle. The check compares `tck` and `trst_n` only from the second cycle of the connection.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_02"></a>REQ_RRAM_02 | <br>While the RRAM TAP is not connected, the TMS and TDI of `rram_jtag_o` shall be 0. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0*. From the release of `rst_ni` on, the check requires `tms` and `tdi` of `rram_jtag_o` to be 0 in every cycle in which the RRAM TAP is cut. The check allows the pads to carry any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_03"></a>REQ_RRAM_03 | <br>The TCK and TRST_N of `rram_jtag_o` shall be 0 during reset and in the `clk_i` cycle after reset. They shall also be 0 in the `clk_i` cycle after any cycle in which the RRAM TAP is not connected. (*RTL*) <br><br>*Sources:* No specification states this rule. Nearest text: [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [pinmux.hjson `clocking`](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *TCK and TRST low after a cut*. The check requires `tck` and `trst_n` of `rram_jtag_o` to be 0 in reset and in the first cycle after reset. The check requires the same in every cycle that follows a cycle in which the RRAM TAP is cut.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_09"></a>REQ_RRAM_09 | <br>In the first `clk_i` cycle in which the RRAM TAP is no longer connected, the TCK and TRST_N of `rram_jtag_o` shall still carry the inputs of the TCK pad and the TRST_N pad. This holds outside reset. (*RTL*: the clock that counts the cycle, and the value of TRST_N) <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [pinmux.hjson `clocking`](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the clock that counts the cycle, and the value of TRST_N.<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *TCK and TRST run one cycle more*. The check applies to each cycle outside reset in which the RRAM TAP is cut and was connected in the cycle before. In such a cycle, the check compares `tck` with the TCK pad and `trst_n` with the TRST_N pad.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_04"></a>REQ_RRAM_04 | <br>In the selection of the RRAM TAP, `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` shall count as On only at the value 4'b0101. <br><br>*Sources:* [Control Signal Propagation](../../../../../ip/lc_ctrl/doc/interfaces.md#control-signal-propagation); [pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` LC_NVM_DEBUG_EN.INTERSIG.MUBI](../../data/pinmux.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *only True and On open*, *cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0*. With `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` free, any held value other than 4'b0101 cuts the RRAM TAP. The check _cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0_ then requires `tms` and `tdi` of `rram_jtag_o` to be 0.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_05"></a>REQ_RRAM_05 | <br>After a reset, the RRAM TAP shall not be connected until software writes `kMultiBitBool4True` to `RRAM_JTAG_SEL`. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *cut until the register is written*. Until the first accepted write to `RRAM_JTAG_SEL`, the check requires `tms` and `tdi` of `rram_jtag_o` to be 0. The check allows the straps and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` to take any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_06"></a>REQ_RRAM_06 | <br>`RRAM_JTAG_SEL` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` shall not change which of the life cycle TAP, the RISC-V TAP and the DFT TAP is connected. They shall not change what that TAP receives either. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [`RRAM_JTAG_SEL`](../registers.md#rram_jtag_sel); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `jtag`: *connected TAP gets the pads*, *cut TAP gets zero*. Both checks cover the requests of the life cycle, RISC-V and DFT TAPs while `RRAM_JTAG_SEL` and `lc_nvm_debug_en_i` are free.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_rram_07"></a>REQ_RRAM_07 | <br>`lc_check_byp_en_i` and the latch shall not change whether the RRAM TAP is connected. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_rram_tap`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `rram_tap`: *RRAM TAP kept through a transition*, *cut RRAM TAP gets TMS and TDI 0*. The check _RRAM TAP kept through a transition_ requires a connected RRAM TAP to stay connected during a life cycle transition or while the latch is Off.<br><br> |
% endif
