${"##"} DFT straps

Security-relevant ([Groups](#groups)).

Conditions:

* The output `dft_strap_test_o` holds a valid bit and the straps.
* The straps take bit 0 from the DFT strap 0 pad and bit 1 from the DFT strap 1 pad ([existing pinmux FPV testplan: DftStrapTestO_A](../../data/pinmux_fpv_testplan.hjson)), two pads that the top description assigns and that the table [Pads by role](#pads-by-role) lists.
* Two documents disagree on the number of DFT strap pads.
* The top description gives two, and the theory of operation gives three ([Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation)).
* The rows follow the top description, because it sets the pads that the pinmux is built with.

Testpoints: [`dft_strap`](../../data/pinmux_env_fpv_testplan.hjson#dft_strap) (V2S, priority 2).

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| <a id="req_dft_01a"></a>REQ_DFT_01a | <br>At a `strap_en_i` pulse, the valid bit of `dft_strap_test_o` shall take the value 1, if `lc_dft_en_i` is On. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)<br><br>*Checked by:* `dft_strap`: *pulse samples DFT straps*. At a strap pulse with `lc_dft_en_i` On in each of the two cycles before, the check requires the valid bit to be 1 from the next cycle on.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dft_01b"></a>REQ_DFT_01b | <br>At a `strap_en_i` pulse, the straps of `dft_strap_test_o` shall take the values of the DFT strap 0 pad and the DFT strap 1 pad, if `lc_dft_en_i` is On. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); [Inter-Module Signals](../interfaces.md#inter-module-signals); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson); [Manufacturing States](../../../../../../doc/security/specs/device_life_cycle/README.md#manufacturing-states)<br><br>*Checked by:* `dft_strap`: *pulse samples DFT straps*. At a strap pulse with `lc_dft_en_i` steadily On, the check compares the two straps after the pulse with the DFT strap 0 pad and the DFT strap 1 pad. The check accepts the value of each pad in the pulse cycle or in the cycle after it.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dft_02a"></a>REQ_DFT_02a | <br>Once the valid bit of `dft_strap_test_o` is 1, the valid bit shall stay 1 until a full reset. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `dft_strap`: *DFT straps held*. Once the valid bit is 1, the check requires the output to keep its value into each next cycle that is not in full reset. The check allows `lc_dft_en_i` and the pads to take any value.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dft_02b"></a>REQ_DFT_02b | <br>Once the valid bit of `dft_strap_test_o` is 1, the straps of `dft_strap_test_o` shall keep their values until a full reset. <br><br>*Sources:* [Strap Sampling and TAP Isolation](../theory_of_operation.md#strap-sampling-and-tap-isolation); ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[Non-debug Module Reset](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey englishbreakfast'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#non-debug-module-reset); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes lc_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `resets.nodes sys_io_div4`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `module.pinmux`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)<br><br>*Checked by:* `dft_strap`: *DFT straps held*. Once the valid bit is 1, the check requires the two straps to keep their values into each next cycle that is not in full reset.<br><br> |
| <a id="req_dft_03"></a>REQ_DFT_03 | <br>`dft_strap_test_o` shall be all 0 before a sample, which takes place at a `strap_en_i` pulse while `lc_dft_en_i` is On. This holds for any value on the DFT strap 0 pad and the DFT strap 1 pad. (*RTL*: the value before the first sample) <br><br>*Sources:* ${'' if topname in 'earlgrey darjeeling'.split() else "Earl Grey's "}[chip_testplan.hjson `chip_sw_tap_strap_sampling`](../../../../../top_${topname if topname in 'earlgrey darjeeling'.split() else 'earlgrey'}/data/chip_testplan.hjson); [top_${topname}.hjson${eg(' `targets.asic.pinmux.special_signals`')}](../../../../data/top_${topname}.hjson); [top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `enable_strap_sampling`](../../data/top_${topname}_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson). No specification states the value before the first sample.<br><br>*Checked by:* `dft_strap`: *zero until sampled*. The check requires every bit of `dft_strap_test_o` to be 0 until a strap pulse at which `lc_dft_en_i` was On in either of the two cycles before.<br><br> |
% endif
